    "why": "npm recorded 619,682,667 downloads of keyv from 5 July to 3 August. npm runs a preinstall script by itself during install, so no one has to import keyv or start an app for the code to run. Reports say its hidden second stage goes after GitHub and npm tokens, cloud credentials and private keys. Developer laptops and CI runners are prized targets because they often hold those credentials."
